# Input
```
-- The table was created in a transaction that committed, so other transactions can see it.
-- expect_lint/constraintMissingNotValid
BEGIN;
CREATE TABLE orders (id bigint, amount int);
COMMIT;
BEGIN;
ALTER TABLE orders ADD CONSTRAINT orders_amount_check CHECK (amount > 0);
COMMIT;

```

# Diagnostics
lint/constraintMissingNotValid  FIXABLE  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × Adding a constraint without NOT VALID will block reads and writes while validating existing rows.
  
  i Add the constraint as NOT VALID in one transaction, then run VALIDATE CONSTRAINT in a separate transaction.
  


## Fix (unsafe): Add NOT VALID
```
-- The table was created in a transaction that committed, so other transactions can see it.
-- expect_lint/constraintMissingNotValid
BEGIN;
CREATE TABLE orders (id bigint, amount int);
COMMIT;
BEGIN;
ALTER TABLE orders ADD CONSTRAINT orders_amount_check CHECK (amount > 0) NOT VALID;
COMMIT;

```
